Name: tokio
License File: LICENSE
Description: An event-driven, non-blocking I/O platform for writing asynchronous applications with the Rust programming language.

* What is this crate used for?
Asynchronous runtime and networking primitives.

* Are there any use restrictions? i.e. only for development hosts
No.

* What differs from upstream? Include a changelog if feasible.
Added `target_os = "fuchsia"` to `impl_noproc` in `src/net/unix/ucred.rs`.
This is filed upstream as pull request in https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/pull/8257.

* Are there any restrictions to how it should be rolled?
Ensure `target_os = "fuchsia"` support for `impl_noproc` or peer creds is preserved.
This can be unforked once a version can be vendored in that contains
https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/pull/8257.

* Is there anything else which makes this dependency "special"?
No.
